Native Windows Build With MSVC
==============================

This build path is additive.  It uses the existing Win32 drawterm backend and
does not replace the Unix, macOS, or MinGW makefiles.

From an x64 Visual Studio 2022 developer shell, run:

	nmake /f NMakefile.msvc

The output executable is:

	build\msvc\drawterm.exe

For diagnostics, set `DRAWTERM_LOG` to a writable file path before running
drawterm. Console output, fatal errors, panics, and unhandled exception details
will be appended to that file. Pass `-v` or set `DRAWTERM_VERBOSE=1` to add
connection and authentication stage tracing.

The helper script `test-msvc-drawterm.ps1` runs the MSVC executable with
diagnostics enabled, waits for it to exit, and prints the captured log:

	.\test-msvc-drawterm.ps1

The script defaults to `-h 127.0.0.1 -a 127.0.0.1 -u glenda` and uses
`$env:PASS`, falling back to `cleartext`. For an interactive manual
test, disable the timeout and close the drawterm window when done:

	.\test-msvc-drawterm.ps1 -TimeoutSeconds 0

Use a positive `-TimeoutSeconds` value to stop a hung test run automatically.

To clean the MSVC build artifacts:

	nmake /f NMakefile.msvc clean

The normal upstream build files remain the source of truth for non-MSVC
targets.
